      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A subungual haematoma is a collection of blood beneath a finger or toe nail. It is often caused by a crush injury (Purcell, 2003) such as shutting a finger in a door or other types of trauma. Heim et al (2000) note that these haematomas can also be caused by repetitive trauma in athletes such as runners and dancers."},
